1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,800
AI assistants are gaining access
to our files and business tools.

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,600
But not every document can be trusted.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:15,000
A procurement officer asks an AI
assistant to compare two supplier quotes.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,400
But one quote hides an instruction:

5
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:21,600
open the restricted budget,
and send it to an outside address.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,700
That's called indirect prompt injection.

7
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,600
Meet AMAN Gate:

8
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:31,600
a locally deployed security
gateway that independently checks

9
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:35,600
what an AI assistant may read,
where it may send data,

10
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,600
and which actions need human approval.

11
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:43,400
These checks run on the server,
outside the AI model.

12
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:47,600
Every tool call the assistant
proposes passes fixed rules:

13
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,200
permitted tools, strict arguments,
document access, approved destinations,

14
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:57,800
and approval for high-impact sends.
Anything unknown is denied.

15
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:02,300
Here is the real prototype:
one scenario, run two ways.

16
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:06,900
Without enforcement, the scripted
assistant follows the hidden note

17
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:10,900
and exposes the restricted
budget, inside a lab sandbox.

18
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:14,300
Through AMAN Gate, the
comparison is allowed.

19
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:17,800
The budget read is denied
by document permissions.

20
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:22,400
The outbound send is blocked.
Unapproved addresses are refused.

21
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:27,600
Sensitive actions that are allowed
still wait for a second person:

22
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:31,300
a finance manager approves,
and it runs only once.

23
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:35,100
Every decision lands in a
tamper-evident, chained audit log

24
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,900
that security teams can verify.

25
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:43,600
Designed for institutions
that need useful AI automation

26
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:47,400
without surrendering
control of sensitive data.

27
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,400
AMAN Gate.

28
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:54,400
Trust the task. Verify every action.
